# ─── Benchmark output (stage 3.1) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ad-hoc eval runs only. The documents, the questions, the gold answers and any
# committed baseline are version-controlled on purpose: Module 3 of
# docs/curriculum.md is explicit that the eval set is "a primary artifact of
# this project, not a side experiment ... it is version-controlled".
#
# Four rules here previously ignored all of it — benchmark/documents/,
# questions/, gold/ and results/ — left over from the pre-pivot product era,
# when the benchmark was an experiment rather than the instrument every later
# claim depends on.
benchmark/runs/

# Frontend env (must not be committed)
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.local
frontend/.env.*.local

# ─── Operational exports (stage 2.2) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# `tools/qdrant_orphans.py` takes the live document list as a file, exported
# from Postgres on the host. It is a snapshot of one moment, so a committed
# copy would be stale the next time anyone ran the tool — and acting on a
# stale list is how a reconciliation tool deletes live data.
live.csv
